Make /v1/audio/transcriptions answer with the timings it already computed.

Applied against AUDIOCPP_REF in Dockerfile.audio (04ba4375). Upstream:
https://github.com/0xShug0/audio.cpp

The problem
-----------
audio.cpp has two ways in for a wav, and only one of them is an upload:

  POST /v1/tasks/run              JSON, "audio" is a path the SERVER opens
  POST /v1/audio/transcriptions   JSON path, or multipart/form-data upload

Both run the same model and produce the same TaskResult -- text, speech
segments, and per-word start_sample/end_sample. But the two serialise it
differently. /v1/tasks/run returns all of it. /v1/audio/transcriptions
hand-built a two-field object and threw the rest away:

    {"text": "...", "timing": {...}}

So the only endpoint that accepts an upload is also the only one that cannot
tell you WHEN anything was said -- which pushes any client that needs word
timings (autocut does: words.json, the transcript scrub, the cut suggestions)
back onto the path-based endpoint, and therefore onto sharing a filesystem
with the server and mounting its project folder into the container.

The change
----------
run_transcription now returns task_result_json_with_timing(), the same
serialiser /v1/tasks/run uses. Three lines of code.

Backwards compatible: "text" is still the first field and still means what it
did; segments/words/language are additive, and a client reading .text (Open
WebUI, anything Whisper-shaped) sees no difference.

Not covered by this patch
-------------------------
Diarization and voice cloning still have no upload route at all -- diar models
are only reachable at /v1/tasks/run, and /v1/audio/speech takes voice_ref as a
server-side path. Dropping the shared mount entirely needs multipart support
on /v1/tasks/run, which is a bigger change than this one.

diff --git a/app/server/runtime.cpp b/app/server/runtime.cpp
index adbf4f3..ae4918e 100644
--- a/app/server/runtime.cpp
+++ b/app/server/runtime.cpp
@@ -1975,9 +1975,14 @@ HttpResponse ServerState::run_transcription(
     if (!request.audio_input.has_value()) {
         throw std::runtime_error("transcription timing requires audio_input");
     }
-    return json_response(
-        "{\"text\":" + json_quote(result.text_output->text) +
-        ",\"timing\":" + timing_json(timed_result.wall_ms, *request.audio_input) + "}");
+    // The same body /v1/tasks/run returns, not a two-field subset of it. An ASR
+    // model produces word_timestamps and speech_segments alongside the text, and
+    // this endpoint used to drop both on the floor -- so a client that uploaded
+    // its audio got a flat string and had to fall back to a server-side path to
+    // learn when anything was said. text stays the first field, and every other
+    // field is additive, so OpenAI-shaped clients read it exactly as before.
+    return json_response(task_result_json_with_timing(
+        result, timing_json(timed_result.wall_ms, *request.audio_input)));
 }
 
 HttpResponse ServerState::run_transcription_stream(
